11. Submodularity Diagnostic

Let E=\{e_1,\ldots,e_K\} and V_H(S)=J_{\varnothing}^*(H)-J_S^*(H). For A\subseteq B and e\notin B, submodularity requires

V_H(A\cup\{e\})-V_H(A)\ge V_H(B\cup\{e\})-V_H(B).

The actuator-selection objectives of LQR/LQG fail exact sub/supermodularity but admit approximate supermodularity [5]. For multiphysics EV coupling removal:

1. Counterexample. A two-subsystem bilinear system with cost x_1^2+x_2^2 violates the diminishing-returns inequality.
2. Approximate submodularity. Under LQ multiphysics with no active constraints, a submodularity-ratio bound \gamma may be derived using curvature tools from the actuator-selection literature.

Either result is publishable.

