16. Provisional Thesis

Existing adjoint sensitivity theory, specialized to block-structured coupling removal, yields a first-order signed value V_e(H) given by the costate-weighted integral of the removed coupling. Under interior-regime assumptions the remainder is quadratic, with explicit constant R_e\le C_R\kappa_e^{\text{tube}\,2}. Whether a quantitatively useful structured constant \gamma_e<1, a Clarke-subdifferential active-set jump estimate, or a submodularity-ratio bound can be obtained remains open.

