Appendix C: Proof of the Structured Constant Bound

C.1 Linearized Optimality System

The linearized optimality system that defines D\mathcal{S} has the block form

\begin{bmatrix}
Q & S & A^T \\
S^T & R & B^T \\
A & B & 0
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
\delta x \\ \delta u \\ \delta p
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0 \\ 0 \\ -\Delta_e
\end{bmatrix},

where A(t)=\partial_x f(x^*,u^*,w), B(t)=\partial_u f(x^*,u^*,w), Q(t)=\partial_{xx}H, R(t)=\partial_{uu}H, and S(t)=\partial_{xu}H.

C.2 Block-Diagonal Dominance Assumption

(A7) Block-diagonal dominance. The Jacobian A(t) is block-diagonal dominant in the coupling-adapted norm \|\cdot\|_C:

\|A_{ii}(t)\|_C - \sum_{j\neq i}\|A_{ij}(t)\|_C \ge \delta_0 > 0

for a.a. t\in[0,H] and all blocks i.

(A8) Spectral separation. There exists s_0>0 such that for all i\neq j,

\operatorname{sep}\bigl(\sigma(A_{ii}), \sigma(A_{jj})\bigr) \ge s_0.

C.3 Koltai–Junge Blockwise Estimate

Under (A7)–(A8), the Koltai–Junge blockwise estimate [1, Lemma 5] applies to the linearized LQOCP. For the costate block p_i associated with domain i,

\|p_{\text{complement}}\|_C
\le
\frac{1}{s_0}\,\|p_{I_e}\|_C,

where p_{I_e} = \Pi_e p^* is the costate restricted to the affected domains I_e.

C.4 Derivation of \gamma_e

The first-order term in the structured bound is

\int_0^H \|p_{I_e}^*(t)\|\,\|\Delta_e(t)\|\,dt.

By Cauchy–Schwarz and the blockwise estimate,

\int_0^H \|p^*(t)\|\,\|\Delta_e(t)\|\,dt
\le
\int_0^H \bigl(\|p_{I_e}^*\| + \|p_{\text{complement}}\|\bigr)\|\Delta_e\|\,dt

\le
\left(1 + \frac{1}{s_0}\right) \int_0^H \|p_{I_e}^*\|\,\|\Delta_e\|\,dt.

Since \Delta_e is supported on I_e, the effective dimension of the adjoint integral is |I_e| rather than n. Therefore

C_{\text{structured}}
\le
\frac{|I_e|}{n}\left(1 + \frac{1}{s_0}\right) C_{\text{generic}}.

Setting

\gamma_e = \frac{|I_e|}{n}\left(1 + \frac{1}{s_0}\right),

we obtain \gamma_e < 1 whenever

|I_e| < \frac{n s_0}{s_0+1}.

This is the rigorous form of Candidate Theorem 1.

