Appendix H: Numerical Tightness Protocol — Detailed Specifications

H.1 Parameter Grid

Let the grid be

\mathcal{G} = \{(H_i, \varepsilon_j, m_{g,k}) : i=1,\ldots,N_H,\; j=1,\ldots,N_\varepsilon,\; k=1,\ldots,N_m\}.

For each grid point, compute:

· the true value V_e(H_i,\varepsilon_j,m_{g,k}) by solving the perturbed optimal control problem;
· the first-order adjoint prediction P_e^{\text{adj}}(H_i);
· the classical Grönwall bound;
· the structured bound C_H P_e^{\text{adj}} + R_e.

H.2 Reporting Requirements

For each grid point, report:

· \kappa_e^{\text{traj}} and \kappa_e^{\text{tube}};
· the separation s_0 from (A8);
· \|\psi_z^{-1}\| from (B1);
· the tightness ratio

\rho = \frac{\text{structured bound}}{\text{true } |V_e|}.

The scientific value lies in showing that \rho is usefully less than the corresponding ratio for the generic Grönwall bound.

H.3 Visualization

Plot \rho as a function of H, \varepsilon, and m_g. The structured bound should be tightest in the interior regime (m_g>0) and degrade gracefully as m_g\to 0.

