Appendix J: Failure Conditions — Formal Statement

The program should be abandoned or redirected if any of the following conditions hold:

(F1) Known result. The structured bound |V_e(H)|\le \mathcal{B}_e(H) is already present in the literature.

(F2) Trivial specialization. The bound follows from an existing theorem without meaningful use of the block-sparse structure of \Delta_e.

(F3) Vacuous constants. The constants C_R, s_0, or \gamma_e are so loose that \mathcal{B}_e(H) exceeds the trivial bound 2\max(J^*,J_e^*).

(F4) No horizon information. The horizon-dependent formulation adds no mathematical information beyond the static bound.

(F5) No EV structure. The EV specialization introduces no new mathematical structure; the framework is a re-labeling of generic sensitivity theory.

In any of these cases, the appropriate scientific action is to document the negative result and not claim novelty.

