Appendix K: Research Sequence — Formal Dependencies

The research program proceeds in the following order:

1. Collision audit formalization. Complete the bibliographic verification of all cited results.
2. Minimal analytical laboratory. Solve the two-subsystem problem exactly; compute \partial J^*/\partial\varepsilon and \partial^2 J^*/\partial\varepsilon^2.
3. Interior-regime bound. Prove the bound under (C1)–(C3), (B1), m_g>0, and (A7)–(A8). If (A7)–(A8) fail, downgrade Candidate Theorem 1 to a conjecture.
4. Active-set jump estimate. Specialize Stechlinski [3] to control constraints; specialize Bettiol–Frankowska–Vinter [4] to state constraints. Express the jump in terms of the projection of \Delta_e onto the normal cone.
5. Submodularity diagnostic. Construct the bilinear counterexample; prove approximate submodularity under LQ assumptions; derive the submodularity ratio bound.
6. Numerical tightness protocol. Implement the protocol of Appendix H on the minimal laboratory and, if the bound survives, on validated ITMS models.
7. EV interpretation. Only after steps 1–6, instantiate on validated EV models with cited physical equations.

